# Set one mixer channel by name ("master", "mic" -- the fields of Mixer.msg).
# Channel-addressed so that setting one channel can never overwrite another,
# and new channels need no interface change. Values outside [0, 1] are
# clamped; the response reports the volume actually applied, so the caller
# can detect clamping by comparing it with the request. An unknown channel
# yields success: false (ROS services have no out-of-band error channel;
# failure is in-band, in the response).
string channel
float32 value   # desired linear volume, clamped to 0.0 .. 1.0
---
bool success    # false for an unknown channel
float32 value   # the volume actually applied, after clamping
